.policy "ruff-f823-undefined-local" revision 1
.guests off
.description "Don't read a variable before the function assigns it, even when an outer scope has the same name; Python raises UnboundLocalError."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"
// Generated from today's JSON by docs/rule-syntax/site/translate.py. Display only: not compiled or run.
// ast(n, {…}) atoms are JSON terms with no .rr form yet; the engine matches them as it does today.

// F823(n): a finding at node n, from clause `undefined-local`.
// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
.violation F823(at: node, n: loc) "Assign `{n}` before reading it here, or declare it `global` or `nonlocal` if you meant the outer variable."
    suppress noqa "F823"
F823(n, N) :- kind(n, "identifier"), node(_, n, _, _, _), N = n,
    ast(n, {"resolves": {"beforeLocal": true}}).
